  "solution": {
    "text": "<p> All the metals except scandium form MO oxides, which are ionic. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Mn</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> is a covalent green oil.  In vanadium there is gradual change from the basic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> to less basic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and to amphoteric <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> . <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> dissolves in acids to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>VO</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> salts. Similarly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> reacts with alkalies as well as acids to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>VO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>VO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math> respectively. The well characterised <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CrO</mi></math> is basic but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is amphoteric.</p><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Mn</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> is green oil at room temperature.</p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> dissolve in acids to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> salts.</p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CrO</mi></math> is basic oxide.</p><p>Hence option B is the answer,</p>",
    "image": null
  },
